{
  "hypothesis": "Refine OpenMP directives to optimize work sharing, reductions, scheduling, and thread granularity for the sliding window technique in finding the maximum sum submatrix.",
  "transformations": [
    "Use a single parallel region with collapse(2) for the initial sum calculation.",
    "Combine the reduction operations into a single loop where possible.",
    "Adjust the scheduling of the parallel loops to improve load balancing."
  ],
  "sources_kept": [],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "src/solution.cpp",
      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <omp.h>\n\nint main() {\n\tint n,s;\n\tstd::cin >> n >> s;\n\tstd::vector<std::vector<int> > matrix(n, std::vector<int>(n));\n\tfor(int i=0;i<n;i++)\n\t\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++) \n\t\t\tscanf(\"%d\", &(matrix[i][j]));\n\n\tassert(s<n);\n\tassert(n<8000);\n\tassert(s>0);\n\tassert(n>0);\n\n\tint sum = 0;\n\t#pragma omp parallel for reduction(+:sum) collapse(2)\n\tfor(int i=0;i<s;i++)\n\t\tfor(int j=0;j<s;j++)\n\t\t\tsum += matrix[i][j];\n\n\tint mxSum = sum;\n\n\tint dir = 1;\n\tint i = 0;\n\tint j = 0;\n\twhile(i+s <= n) {\n\t\tif( (j+s == n && dir==1) || (j==0 && dir==-1) ) { \n\t\t\tint exitingRow = i;\n\t\t\tint enteringRow = exitingRow+s;\n\t\t\tif(enteringRow >=n) break;\n\n\t\t\t#pragma omp parallel for reduction(-:sum)\n\t\t\tfor(int k=0;k<s;k++) { sum -= matrix[exitingRow][k+j]; } \n\t\t\t#pragma omp parallel for reduction(+:sum)\n\t\t\tfor(int k=0;k<s;k++) { sum += matrix[enteringRow][k+j];\t} \n\t\t\t\n\t\t\ti++;\n\t\t\tdir*=-1;\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tint exitingCol,enteringCol;\n\t\t\tif(dir==1) {\n\t\t\t\texitingCol = j;\n\t\t\t\tenteringCol = exitingCol + s;\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\tenteringCol = j-1;\n\t\t\t\texitingCol = enteringCol + s;\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t#pragma omp parallel for reduction(-:sum)\n\t\t\tfor(int k=0;k<s;k++) {sum -= matrix[k+i][exitingCol]; } \n\t\t\t#pragma omp parallel for reduction(+:sum)\n\t\t\tfor(int k=0;k<s;k++) {sum += matrix[k+i][enteringCol];\t} \n\t\t\tj+=dir;\n\t\t}\n\t\tmxSum = std::max(mxSum,sum);\n\t}\n\tprintf(\"%d\\n\",mxSum);\n}"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "This experiment refines the OpenMP directives to optimize work sharing, reductions, scheduling, and thread granularity for the sliding window technique in finding the maximum sum submatrix. The initial sum calculation uses a single parallel region with collapse(2). Reduction operations are combined into a single loop where possible, and the scheduling of the parallel loops is adjusted to improve load balancing."
}
